herdr guide 2: panes, tabs and copy mode
========================================

After herdr-1-basics. Day-to-day editing of the layout.

PANES
  <prefix> S-h/j/k/l              Swap the pane left/down/up/right
  <prefix> r                      Resize mode (follow the hints on screen)
  <prefix> tab / <prefix> S-tab   Cycle panes
  <prefix> S-p                    Rename the pane
  <prefix> e                      Open the scrollback in $EDITOR (search and copy long
                                  output there)

TABS AND WORKSPACES
  <prefix> S-t                    Rename the tab
  <prefix> S-x                    Close the tab
  <prefix> S-w                    Rename the workspace
  <prefix> S-d                    Close the workspace
  <prefix> S-g                    New git worktree workspace

COPY MODE
  <prefix> [                      Enter copy mode. Output stays live while you scroll
  h/j/k/l, w/b/e, W/B/E           Move
  C-u / C-d                       Half page up / down
  PageUp / PageDown               Page up / down (C-b is the prefix, so it does not page up)
  / or ?                          Search forward / backward, then n / N to repeat
  v or Space                      Start a selection
  y or Enter                      Copy and leave
  q or Esc                        Leave without copying
  Mouse drag                      Copy without copy mode

GOTO PICKER (<PREFIX> G)
  /                               Search names, agent kinds, tabs, workspaces, branches,
                                  paths
  j/k or Up/Down                  Move between rows
  Left/Right                      Previous / next workspace section
  b/w/i/d                         Show only blocked / working / idle / done agents
  a                               Show all terminals again
  Enter                           Jump to the row

SETTINGS
  <prefix> s                      Open settings
  <prefix> S-r                    Reload config
